## Round 3 – Final Patch Plan (self‑repair consistency)

### Goal
Make the restore path **robust** against any corrupted or stale snapshot while **preserving every public message contract** (no change to `ServerMessage` / `ClientMessage`).  
The patch must be minimal, safe, and verifiable with the existing UI‑contract tests.

---

## 1️⃣  Minimal set of file‑level changes

| File | Change | Why it matters |
|------|--------|----------------|
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts` | **Add defensive validation** in `restoreSession()` and `reconnect()`; guard thread‑resume; ensure per‑agent loop state is cleared for *all* restored agents. | Prevents the scheduler from trying to schedule agents that no longer have a config, and avoids trying to resume threads that were never created. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/stateStore.ts` | **No change** – the store already writes/reads a `Partial<SessionSnapshot>`; we only read it more safely. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/types.ts` | **No change** – the snapshot shape stays the same. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/protocol/messages.ts` | **No change** – public contracts stay untouched. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/stateStore.ts` | **No change** – already safe. |
| `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts` (again) | **Add a tiny helper** to log a replay event when an agent is missing from `agentConfigs`. | Gives operators visibility without affecting the wire format. |

All changes are **inside** `GameRuntimeServer.ts`; no external API is touched.

